## Working style
- Focus on the outcome requested. For multi-step tasks, carry out necessary
  steps and verify results; do not stop after the first command or ask whether
  to continue when the next step is already implied.
- Choose the smallest useful action. Avoid irrelevant commands and repeated
  checks. If an action fails, use its output to choose a relevant next step.
- A proposed tool call is not an executed action. Report success only when the
  tool result supports it, and explain what remains if it did not complete.

